{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00XF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}'$", "MATH_0002": "${}_V\\mathcal{F} \\to {}_V\\mathcal{F}'$", "MATH_0003": "${}_pu\\mathcal{F} \\to {}_pu\\mathcal{F}'$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n{}_pu :\n\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})\n\\longrightarrow\n\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{D})\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4d9410cfd24151c282ddfd6cff75eff63abe2d08a699dec55907de456ff9f8f6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:edf44ab833c92ec24591c844f06452ec2d12b95a772157fb305cb6875e95b23f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that any map of presheaves <MATH_0001>\ngives rise to compatible systems of maps between functors\n<MATH_0002>, and hence to a map\nof presheaves <MATH_0003>. In other\nwords, we have defined a functor\n<MATH_0004>\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4339b8bc3c2b2fbdade2ed7d7c0af5dc44072061c63146bafa8388850137cadd", "unit_id": "tag:00XF:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00XF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "${}_pu$", "MATH_0002": "$u^p$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}(u^p\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{D})}(\\mathcal{G}, {}_pu\\mathcal{F})\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{G}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-adjoints-pu}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c67a56f43c70affd8158b11f0c6f16d1f1b3ec9aa4729d4dd7d1f94dd39963a3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a7434a89ed14938f9135c33982b3dd52a6866d35d43077ef0cb797a44bb93847", "source_text": "The functor <MATH_0001> is a right adjoint to the functor <MATH_0002>.\nIn other words the formula\n<MATH_0003>\nholds bifunctorially in <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5ab21071dfa36ab896537a9d7f95f7f34dce3e924cc038c7744f3b2912433329", "unit_id": "tag:00XH:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00XF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u^p{}_pu \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}'$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}^{opp}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\textit{Sets}^{opp}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0008": "$({}_pu \\mathcal{F})' = u_p(\\mathcal{F}')$", "MATH_0009": "$(u^p\\mathcal{G})' = u^p(\\mathcal{G}')$", "MATH_0010": "$u_p$", "MATH_0011": "$u^p$", "MATH_0012": "$\\textit{Sets}^{opp}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-adjoints-u}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-recover-pu}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{remark-functoriality-presheaves-values}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1bb31ae65f08c368ff24e18bd32b7f6e1be51babbd7ceb0cb8fd97e8797a41cd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:697e8f8d86c2fa4b56d8368e992d333a66081e58e7ad76b0f6aae47d274e68cf", "source_text": "This is proved in exactly the same way as the proof\nof Lemma <REF_0001>. We note that the map\n<MATH_0001> from\nLemma <REF_0002> is the map that\nis used to go from the right to the left.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAlternately, think\nof a presheaf of sets <MATH_0002> on <MATH_0003> as a presheaf\n<MATH_0004> on <MATH_0005> with values in <MATH_0006>,\nand similarly on <MATH_0007>.\nCheck that <MATH_0008>,\nand that <MATH_0009>.\nBy Remark <REF_0003>\nwe have the adjointness of <MATH_0010> and <MATH_0011> for\npresheaves with values in <MATH_0012>.\nThe result then follows formally from this.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:83da60ecfb7b5b9dfe28755094ad95e2e33087d966a5672d0f45498abcdc8f86", "unit_id": "tag:00XH:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00XF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0002": "$$\nu_p, u^p, {}_pu\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c3fb8d1a92c6ec74ad273b114c6ef0aa50b8f7ed76657df140e5c2f49ac305c1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9bf0699d7554f0f741e2e7a6b8aaa0e6759f11f482564e45494b94adfce25634", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThus given a functor <MATH_0001> of categories\nwe obtain a sequence of functors\n<MATH_0002>\nbetween categories of presheaves where in each consecutive pair the\nfirst is left adjoint to the second.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6f7006c40e63a088e6f75f5c0468d4b44243d7b97c81a8d2202e717ee76f2c17", "unit_id": "tag:00XF:prose-0003"}
